tate.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-42663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following values is in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/assets/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The domain of the function is $[-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, of the given values, only $x=\\frac{1}{5}$ is in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c2d78be08212e8d1165bf285925564cf6bf7e18e93b3f4b4b460ca7b58fdc3c"} {"question" "q-65939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$\n\n- $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n- $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n- $(1,0)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First, we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{1}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(1,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c2d78be08212e8d1165bf285925564cf6bf7e18e93b3f4b4b460ca7b58fdc3c"} {"question" "q-65947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006797/state.json" "file_sha256" "55acc2980c4363d86e29d67f59aeba9493a2201c04a65ba2b7e3387e6a550997"} {"question" "q-65947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_c